{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss Calibri;}{\f1\fmodern Courier New;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red60\green60\blue60;\red232\green232\blue232;}\fs22\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn{\b\fs40 Building a Real-Time, Photorealistic Avatar with a Generated Voice}\par
\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn{\b\fs30 A practical guide, current to 4 October 2026}\par
\pard\sa120 {\b How this guide was produced.} Eight large language models were asked how to build a real-time rendered photorealistic avatar with a generated voice. Every concrete claim in their answers was checked against primary sources (papers, repositories, licence files, vendor and engine documentation). This guide keeps what survived that check, drops what did not, and adds the corrections. Where a statement is a judgement rather than a verified fact, it is marked as such. Dates matter in this field: several products the models recommended no longer exist.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\sa120\par
\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn{\b\fs30 1. Decide these first}\par
\pard\sa120 Everything else follows from six questions. Answer them before choosing tools.\par
