\pard\sa120 For a locked talking-head framing, viseme timestamps from the TTS are competitive with neural lip-sync at a fraction of the cost. Reach for Audio2Face or a neural model when you need emotional range or a moving camera.\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\sa120\par
\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn{\b\fs30 8. Legal and licensing checklist}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}{\b Engine.} Unreal: free under one million dollars of revenue; 1,850 dollars per seat per year for non-game companies above it. MetaHuman characters may be used in other engines; OpenRigLogic is MIT.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}{\b Models.} Check weights separately from code. Non-commercial: XTTS-v2, F5-TTS weights, Fish Speech, Wav2Lip, InsightFace models (and therefore stock LivePortrait). Permissive: MuseTalk, Ditto, Kokoro, Piper, CosyVoice 2, Orpheus, Chatterbox, Zonos, Sesame CSM, LatentSync, MOVA.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}{\b Likeness and voice.} Written consent covering cloning, synthetic media, permitted uses, duration and revocation; secure storage of voice assets.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}{\b Disclosure.} The EU AI Act's Article 50 transparency rules (chatbot disclosure, deepfake labelling) apply from 2 August 2026. Biometric data rules under GDPR and Illinois BIPA apply when the avatar is a real person. Consider C2PA provenance marks.\par
\pard\sa120
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\sa120\par
\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn{\b\fs30 9. What to build, by scenario}\par
\pard\sa120 {\b Web product, live fast, head-and-shoulders.} LiveKit Agents or Pipecat, Deepgram STT, a fast LLM, Cartesia or ElevenLabs TTS, and a hosted avatar (Tavus, Simli, Anam, HeyGen, Synthesia). Swap the avatar vendor later; the orchestration is the durable part.\par
\pard\sa120 {\b Own IP, full control, body and scene, kiosk or installation.} UE5 plus MetaHuman plus Audio2Face-3D (regression model) or MetaHuman Animator real-time audio, plus streaming TTS (Azure if you want free visemes), plus Pixel Streaming for remote clients. Spend the budget on captured idle, listening and gesture performance from a real actor, not on more shader work.\par
\pard\sa120 {\b A specific real person, maximum realism, cheap to run.} Capture two to three minutes of video, train a Gaussian-splat head (or a per-person 2D model such as MuseTalk over a base loop) and drive it from Audio2Face or FLAME parameters. More engineering, lowest per-minute cost, best realism; accept research-grade tooling.\par
\pard\sa120 {\b Lowest possible latency.} A speech-to-speech model (OpenAI Realtime or Gemini Live) feeding Audio2Face-3D and any renderer, with a short lookahead and matched audio delay.\par
\pard\sa120 {\b A six-week plan for the engine route.}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80 1.\tab Weeks 1 to 2: voice and brain. Streaming STT, LLM with clause chunking, streaming TTS with timestamps, measured end to end at the 95th percentile.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80 2.\tab Weeks 2 to 3: the face. MetaHuman in UE5; drive it from TTS visemes first, then add Audio2Face-3D regression; verify audio-video offset stays inside the ITU window.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80 3.\tab Weeks 3 to 4: liveness and interruption. Idle library, blinks, saccades, look-at; barge-in that flushes every queue.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80 4.\tab Weeks 4 to 5: delivery. Pixel Streaming or native build, NVENC settings, TURN servers, one GPU per session measured.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80 5.\tab Week 6: hardening. Session timeouts, cost per active minute, consent and disclosure flows, failure tests on teeth, tongue, hair edges, long sessions.\par
\pard\sa120
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\sa120\par
\pard\sb240\sa120\keepn{\b\fs30 10. Mistakes to avoid (all observed in the model answers)}\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Treating LivePortrait as a per-person trained model. It is one-shot.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Expecting OpenAI's TTS to return visemes or timestamps. It does not; Azure, Polly and Cartesia do.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Planning on Unity HDRP in a browser. HDRP is not supported on WebGL; URP is.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Calling Audio2Photoreal a Gaussian-splat avatar or a talking-head driver. It is Meta's audio-to-gesture model rendered with Codec Avatars.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Attributing OmniAvatar to Sony or to 3DGS. It is a Zhejiang University and Alibaba audio-driven video-generation model.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Classing Nerfies as Gaussian splatting (it is a 2021 deformable NeRF), FaceX-Zoo as a lip-sync model (it is a face-recognition toolbox), EMO or Loopy as 3D head drivers (they are 2D video diffusion), or RVC as text-to-speech (it is voice conversion).\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Using Rhubarb Lip Sync for live audio. It is an offline command-line tool over recorded files.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Claiming "generating video frames is too slow for real time." MuseTalk, Ditto and SyncTalk run at 30 to 50 fps.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Saying Audio2Face-3D "needs per-character training" or "outputs 100-plus blendshapes." It retargets by blendshape solving and outputs 46 or 52 ARKit blendshapes.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Recommending Ready Player Me or Hedra's realtime avatar. Both were discontinued in 2026.\par
\pard\fi-360\li720\sa80{\pntext\'b7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf0\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'b7}}Quoting the five-percent Unreal royalty as the only cost. Non-game companies above one million dollars pay a per-seat licence.\par
\pard\sa120
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brsp20\sa120\par
